890310502,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA1MDI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:import","name":"topic:import","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-28T19:59:45Z","updated_at":"2025-12-01T13:59:50Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in v4.5.stable.arch_linux\n\n### System information\n\nArch Linux\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen having a texture that is not a power of two and is set to be vram compressed, the Region Editor for `AtlasTexture` has issues displaying the grid over individual pixels, which results in a desync of the grid and the underlying texture pixels\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nImport a Texture that is not PoT, for example 1027x1027. Import it as \"Vram Compressed\".\nAdd a new Resource that is of type `AtlasTexture`.\nEdit the Region of the Atlas Texture with the aforementioned texture set as `atlas`.\nObserve how the Region editor with a grid size of 1x1 does not cover the pixel edges near the center of the texture.\n\n<img width=\"1027\" height=\"1027\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8ee0379d-c05e-4075-aa3c-091572623e0b\" />\n\n<img width=\"1003\" height=\"599\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a7ba58c-30e9-4140-98da-47e94db5bf14\" />\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23829147/mrp.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113294/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"con